{
  "name": "Headless",
  "comment": "The browser off-screen: headless Chromium rendering one page, DevTools over its pipe (fd 3 and 4), no port. It starts\nblank, at its default size: the page and the size are the caller's to give, over the pipe — never on this command line.\nHeadless Chromium says \"HeadlessChrome\" in its user agent and bot checks (Cloudflare) stop there, so it says a normal one.\nTrusted by origin (579): the program, its flags and environment are named here, with only the app's own anchor\n%!app.AbsolutePath%.",
  "step": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "start terminal '//usr/lib/chromium/chromium' with parameters '--headless', '--disable-gpu', '--hide-scrollbars',\n'--no-first-run', '--no-default-browser-check', '--user-data-dir=%!app.AbsolutePath%/.browser',\n'--remote-debugging-pipe',\n'--user-agent=Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/154.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',\n'about:blank', with a clean environment, copying HOME from plang's environment,\nkeep running, with pipe, write to %program%",
      "line": {
        "number": 7
      },
      "code": [
        {
          "module": "terminal",
          "name": "open",
          "property": [
